Wednesday, August 18 is the official last day for business at St. George’s restaurant and Pantry in Lake Grove (see map.) This landmark Victoria restaurant has been a favourite with gastronomes since opening to the public as early as 1938. The business has been expanding and evolving to meet with the ever changing tastes and demands of its clientele for over a quarter century. A small family operated country restaurant was transformed into an “Avenue Cafe” in the '70s, adding to a space a new kitchen, dining room, and bar area; named after Queen Victoria this place became “where breakfast meets lunch.” It later morphed to include an excellent, full service dinner menu which also featured a lovely selection of beer and spirits. Recently added has been several private dining rooms; each equipped with large screen televisions, Internet access, and facilities accommodating large meetings

